  "text": "A broad framework for analyzing thin‑sheet elastic behavior under large deformations of uniform materials is presented. The development starts from a fully general coordinate description and does not limit the form of the stored‑energy function. After assuming that stresses act only within the sheet, the three‑dimensional equations are reduced to a two‑dimensional set, which can be written using complex‑number based functions. When an exact solution is not available, an iterative approximation scheme—similar to that used for the analogous thick‑body case—is introduced. The displacement and stress fields are expressed through complex potentials, and the iteration is stopped after the terms of second order are obtained. The formulation is first given in terms of coordinates attached to the deformed configuration, and then transferred to the original configuration by a simple change of variables. The same approximation ideas are applied to compressible materials under the alternative stress condition, showing that the second‑order results have comparable forms, allowing a unified second‑order theory for two‑dimensional elastic problems."
